
Aztec leverages ZK-SNARKs to enable private computation. This allows transactions and smart contract logic to remain encrypted while still being verified by the network.

Core components:

Private State: balances, variables, and internal contract data remain encrypted.

Public State: settlement, validation, and proofs are published to Ethereum.

Hybrid Execution Model: developers choose which functions are public or private.

By separating private and public states, Aztec offers Ethereum compatibility + privacy guarantees on a single rollup.
